% flatzinc.md's first obligation, and the sharpest one. array_int_element
% becomes an ITE chain, and the chain's final `else` has to denote SOMETHING --
% so without `1 <= i <= |as|` it silently defines as[i] for an out-of-range i,
% a value the model never gave it and one a solver is free to choose.
array [1..3] of int: a = [10, 20, 30];
var 1..3: i;
var int: o;
constraint array_int_element(i, a, o);
solve satisfy;
